cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vfife in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "vfife: an explicit co-rotational finite element solver (VFIFE) in Python"
type: software
version: 1.23.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/maolin2000/vfife"
authors:
  - name: maolin2000
    email: mltianzju@gmail.com
keywords:
  - finite element
  - vector form intrinsic finite element
  - explicit dynamics
  - dynamic relaxation
  - co-rotational
  - fibre beam
  - reinforced concrete
abstract: >-
  A config-driven explicit co-rotational finite element core: continuum
  (hexa8/tet4/tet10/wedge/pyramid/hexa20) on NumPy, Numba and Warp/CUDA
  backends, plus truss, 3-D frame, fibre beam, shell, cable and connector
  line elements, embedded and bonded reinforcement, prestressing tendons,
  moving loads, temperature, creep, shrinkage and relaxation, bearings on the
  fibre beam, seismic base excitation, form-finding, modal analysis and
  fracture with separation on frames, and a verification-contract test suite against published
  experiments and NAFEMS benchmarks.
